{"extract": "James Stephen Wharton, Baron Wharton of Yarm (born 16 February 1984) is a British Conservative Party politician. He was the Member of Parliament (MP) for his home constituency of Stockton South from the 2010 general election, until losing his seat in the 2017 general election. Wharton was appointed Minister for the Northern Powerhouse after his re-election in 2015 and moved to a ministerial position in the Department for International Development by Theresa May in 2016. In September 2020, he took his seat as a member of the House of Lords, taking the title Baron Wharton of Yarm.", "links": [{"ns": 10, "title": "Template:Infobox officeholder", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "2010 United Kingdom general election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "2017 United Kingdom general election", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Alma mater", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Andrew Percy", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Boris Johnson", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Conservative Party (UK)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "County Durham", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Dari Taylor", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "David Behan", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "David Cameron", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Department for Communities and Local Government", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "House of Lords", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Life peer", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Liz Truss", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Lord Temporal", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Member of Parliament (UK)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Member of the House of Lords", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Michael Barber (educationist)", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Nick Hurd", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Office for Students", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Parliamentary Under-Secretary of State for International Development", "exists": true}, {"ns": 0, "title": "Paul Willia